For those of you who tuned in late, SNAP.COM is a memory resident utility
which allows instant text screen saving, retrieval and swapping on most
ms-dos systems.  I wrote it so I could play nethack at work, and immediately
make my screen look legit if someone less hip to creative programming minds
walked by.

I have sent many of you the source already, but someone pointed out that
not everyone has an assembler handy.  Point taken!  From now on, your
handy dandy +2 TSR of stealth kit will contain the following:

SNAP.DOC	brief instructions for use
SNAP.ASM	the source
SNAP.COM	the executable
(I can send just SNAP.COM if you already have the source, or don't want it.)

All three files are very short.

	Interestingly, SNAP has proved so legitimately useful to me on the
job that I almost bragged to the boss about it -- but then I realized that
to do so would be to lose a most valuable secret weapon!!

					The Other David
